  "status": "Complete: exact eight-row single-vector products, exact/reference checks, one Inkling timing and shared-engine regression passed",
  "implementation": [
    "For a single activation vector, compute eight quantized weight rows together with eight independent four-lane F64 accumulator registers",
    "Widen each activation once for all eight rows, exposing independent arithmetic while retaining each row\u2019s original lane sequence and 2048-element span folding",
    "Decode eight rows through the existing Q.Decode_Blocks into a fixed 64-KiB span workspace, with 256 bytes of lane results and 64 bytes of totals; compiler estimates a 66080-byte bounded frame",
    "Apply only under the existing x86-64-v3/FMA guard to Q4_K/Q5_K/Q6_K/Q5_0/Q8_0, non-interleaved whole-block rows and Count=1; leftover rows keep existing execution",
    "Preserve independent row refusals, physical weight ownership and batch execution; no persistent cache, precision change, model-loop change or new runtime/threads"
  ],
  "changed_source_files": [
    "src/library/model_runner-tensors.adb",
    "tests/src/tests-gguf_cases.adb"
  ],
  "focused_aunit": {
    "gguf_and_kernels": "81/81",
    "native_inkling": "15/15"
  },
  "exact_test": "Five-format old-row/batched-row comparisons cover row counts 1\u20139/15/16/17, counts 1\u201315/31/32/33/127/128/129, partial row ranges, shifted bounds, unaligned weights and untouched outputs. Extreme-input scalar comparisons include Count=1 at 2/3/5/8/9/16/17 rows, 256/2048/2304 columns, maximum finite inputs, subnormals, cancellation and signed zeros; the existing paired and triple batch kernels remain covered.",
  "equivalence_domain": "The existing exact FMA argument applies to finite widened binary32 multiplicands; lane and span reductions retain their original order. No NaN payload equivalence claim.",
